Z||000000||jerpro||12-07-2000||03:56 AM||||AS we have all done at one time or another, I had a blind date last night. (first error)<BR>MY friend told me that she was a "nice" girl (second error)<BR>By the time I found out where she lived I had wasted a 1/4 tank of gas, then she lives out in a farm so I had to go through this muddy driveway (third error) in a nice and shiny recently-washed fiero. <BR>I finally get to the front door and this girl that must of wheighed at least 250 pounds comes out to the door. I could not believe my eyes. I had NO Idea how to fit her in the fiero. She finally got in and then we spent the next 10 minutes trying to get the seatbelt on her (you all know how it goes....).<BR>AS we are heading out to the road I remember that the only way back out is through THE DREADED DRIVEWAY. ( I promise you, If I have ever have prayed fervently it was at that precise moment).<BR>MAN!!! it was like carrying a huge mule in the car. I could not look at my right mirror without having to move my head forward away from her breasts. It was horrible.<BR>My fiero didn't like her either because it hesitated and seemed out-of-breath.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>After one movie, 50 pounds of ground beef (me 1/2 a pound, her the rest) and two milk shakes I decided to take her back home. I was so anxious to take her back that I sped a little too much and THE COPS PULLED ME OVER!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> And to make things worse... she started crying!!!<BR>Of course, everyone knows that the early fieros had no glove boxes, so I keep my vehicle registration and insurance in a leather case BEHIND THE PASSENGER SEAT!!!!!!<BR>YOu can gust picture it. A coky cop (in his 20's) a 250 pund girl in a fiero, and ME trying to help her out of the car in the curb so I could get to the registration.<BR>So I finally drop her off and head home.<BR>And just before I get home and think that things could not be worse, I run out of gas!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>luckily the gas station was close by and I was able to push the car over there. <BR>I finally get home, frustrated and everything go to bed and try to forget about all that had happened. <BR>This morning I wake up and take off the snow accumulated over night off my car and.... the paint in the front bumper is cracked and peeling off!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>GRRR.......<BR>I just had to let it out somewhere...<BR>Anyone else with bad experiences?<BR> <BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||RaeQwan||12-07-2000||04:09 AM||||All our prayers are for your car and its quick and painless recovery from its horrible night. May the Cargods bless you for your unliked and eventful night.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwancfa.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000002||RossT||12-07-2000||04:09 AM||||Go rent the movie "blind date" and you will feel a little better.<P>I am sorry, but I couldn't stop laughing!! I am so glad that I am married and (hopefully) don't have to worry about the "dating thing"<BR>every again. I got a wife that lets me buy anything I want for the fiero.<P>keep trying!! don't give up!! your sole mate is out there!!  (somewhere). And maybee, if your lucky, when you find her, SHE WILL LIKE FIEROS!<P>As far as your date goes, remember she has feelings too and you might want to call her and explain that your sorry things didn't work out. It might make you feel better.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ArmandoP||12-07-2000||04:12 AM||||I feel for you man...Ive had MANY days like that...I came outside from pulling an all nighter oine night...kinda like tonight, and found3, THREE!!!!! new dents on my car!  I was soooo pissed....luckily for me my passengers never weigh 250 pounds.....imagine trying to autox with that kind of weight on your passenger side!<BR>dont worry man, it'll get better.<BR>Armando||||reg||1
